From 7f31786cc73fdc8a5c49eadf50776e4bf5fe35d6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andy1210 <andy1210@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 08:45:49 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 041/149] drm/msm/a6xx: Force the GMU off after a GPU_SET OOB
 timeout

When the GMU does not acknowledge the GPU_SET OOB in hw_init(), the
next a6xx_gmu_stop() still takes the graceful path:
a6xx_gmu_shutdown() first repeats the GPU_SET handshake (needs_hw_init
is still set), times out again and only then falls back to
a6xx_gmu_force_off(). Mark the GMU hung right away, as the GMU fault
interrupts do, so that recovery halts the CM3, resets the GPU and
stops the RSC without talking to a GMU that is not answering.
gmu->hung is cleared again by a6xx_gmu_resume().

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_gpu.c | 10 +++++++++-
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_gpu.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_gpu.c
index 081e79ea4652..372542ba1a67 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_gpu.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_gpu.c
@@ -1188,8 +1188,16 @@ static int hw_init(struct msm_gpu *gpu)
 	if (!adreno_has_gmu_wrapper(adreno_gpu)) {
 		/* Make sure the GMU keeps the GPU on while we set it up */
 		ret = a6xx_gmu_set_oob(&a6xx_gpu->gmu, GMU_OOB_GPU_SET);
-		if (ret)
+		if (ret) {
+			/*
+			 * The GMU did not bring GX up: treat it as hung, so
+			 * that the next stop (recovery) forces it off instead
+			 * of a graceful shutdown that starts with another
+			 * GPU_SET handshake.
+			 */
+			gmu->hung = true;
 			return ret;
+		}
 	}
 
 	/* Clear GBIF halt in case GX domain was not collapsed */
